(4943348, 715678, 32345, '<td valign="top">Hi Dave, congrats for your first ribbon and a beautiful picture. :)</td>', 'Hi Dave, congrats for your first ribbon and a beautiful picture. :)', '2008-09-08 22:50:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943351, 716717, 32345, '<td valign="top">A wonderful shot, congrats for the ribbon :)</td>', 'A wonderful shot, congrats for the ribbon :)', '2008-09-08 22:51:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943355, 716202, 39427, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7 and enjoyed this pic.  I think it scored lower than a 6 (unfairly so, IMO) b/c the details in the trees and bushes looks too fuzzy and granulated somehow, and b/c of the slightly unrealistic color scheme.  It just has too much Magenta in it, perhaps this could it could be fixed by setting a ''black point'' with the eye dropper in curves.  Or by going into selective color and going into the neutrals and pumping more black into them.  I like ''unrealistic'' shots and i think the composition is just great here, but somehow it looks like there is an accidental magenta cast rather than a deliberate attempt at making the picture magenta.  Still, I would have pegged this at a 6.3 i don''t get how it scored so low!</td>', 'I gave this a 7 and enjoyed this pic.  I think it scored lower than a 6 (unfairly so, IMO) b/c the details in the trees and bushes looks too fuzzy and granulated somehow, and b/c of the slightly unrealistic color scheme.  It just has too much Magenta in it, perhaps this could it could be fixed by setting a ''black point'' with the eye dropper in curves.  Or by going into selective color and going into the neutrals and pumping more black into them.  I like ''unrealistic'' shots and i think the composition is just great here, but somehow it looks like there is an accidental magenta cast rather than a deliberate attempt at making the picture magenta.  Still, I would have pegged this at a 6.3 i don''t get how it scored so low!', '2008-09-08 22:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943366, 716617, 32345, '<td valign="top">Hello Andi<br/>Wow, look at that, we each had an owl and we both finish in top ten :) <br/>Congrats, it''s a very very nice picture.</td>', 'Hello AndiWow, look at that, we each had an owl and we both finish in top ten :) Congrats, it''s a very very nice picture.', '2008-09-08 22:58:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943387, 716693, 77537, '<td valign="top">my friend CUTOUT asked me to make this comment, what he cant do himself<br/>because he is suspended at the moment<br/> <br/>YOU ARE GREAT</td>', 'my friend CUTOUT asked me to make this comment, what he cant do himselfbecause he is suspended at the moment YOU ARE GREAT', '2008-09-08 23:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943403, 716202, 3936, '<td valign="top">This is a very pretty photo.  At the same time, there is just so much here for an image this size.  If this were a travel poster taking up a good portion of a wall, it could work much better.<br/> <br/>The colors are beautiful, but the picture is very busy and at this scale there is a lot of competition going on.<br/> <br/>The stream tries to act as a leading line.  But it is broken up a bit upstream by the rocks, and the brilliant colors along the stream side, pull the eye away.  When the eye gets to the waterfall, the sky immediately pulls the eye away.  It is hard for the eye to rest on a focal point anywhere in this picture.  Is it the stream, the waterfall, the clouds that I am supposed to look at?  All are competing for a starring role, as opposed to supporting each other.<br/> <br/>Again, the picture itself as a whole is beautiful.  If the scale were larger, it would surely come across better.<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is a very pretty photo.  At the same time, there is just so much here for an image this size.  If this were a travel poster taking up a good portion of a wall, it could work much better. The colors are beautiful, but the picture is very busy and at this scale there is a lot of competition going on. The stream tries to act as a leading line.  But it is broken up a bit upstream by the rocks, and the brilliant colors along the stream side, pull the eye away.  When the eye gets to the waterfall, the sky immediately pulls the eye away.  It is hard for the eye to rest on a focal point anywhere in this picture.  Is it the stream, the waterfall, the clouds that I am supposed to look at?  All are competing for a starring role, as opposed to supporting each other. Again, the picture itself as a whole is beautiful.  If the scale were larger, it would surely come across better. ', '2008-09-08 23:21:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943408, 715430, 30982, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot and congrats on the top ten in a FS - nothing new for you, I know, but a remarkable achievement to repeat that feat so often!  Thanks also for sharing your processing steps!</td>', 'Lovely shot and congrats on the top ten in a FS - nothing new for you, I know, but a remarkable achievement to repeat that feat so often!  Thanks also for sharing your processing steps!', '2008-09-08 23:23:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943431, 708372, 60698, '<td valign="top">Adore this!</td>', 'Adore this!', '2008-09-08 23:32:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943434, 716202, 14369, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image....a little bit saturated and purple... I actually like the HDR version better.<br/> <br/>This version is not very realistic due to the odd colors. If adjusted a little bit more...you would have an even better image!</td>', 'Beautiful image....a little bit saturated and purple... I actually like the HDR version better. This version is not very realistic due to the odd colors. If adjusted a little bit more...you would have an even better image!', '2008-09-08 23:35:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943435, 714173, 63218, '<td valign="top">I think you should try it again, if he will let you.  All that''s wrong with this is it looks tentative. IMHO.  One of those smooth-on, peel-off beauty masks would protect his skin from the dye in the face-paint. Pose him against a white BG that matches his eye-whites, &amp; don''t let his natural skin color show. Maybe work out your lighting in advance to light the black separately from the red. Later, you can work it up to look like a cover for Rolling Stone Magazine or something. "D</td>', 'I think you should try it again, if he will let you.  All that''s wrong with this is it looks tentative. IMHO.  One of those smooth-on, peel-off beauty masks would protect his skin from the dye in the face-paint. Pose him against a white BG that matches his eye-whites, & don''t let his natural skin color show. Maybe work out your lighting in advance to light the black separately from the red. Later, you can work it up to look like a cover for Rolling Stone Magazine or something. "D', '2008-09-08 23:35:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943436, 716202, 40355, '<td valign="top">It''s a very pretty shot, but it''s lacking something in terms of lighting - seems kind of flat to me.  I gave it a 6, so it was above average, but there''s a lack of contrast overall.  Perhaps a little dodging and burning would do the trick.  I sometimes have this same problem with my own photos - they just don''t pop well enough.</td>', 'It''s a very pretty shot, but it''s lacking something in terms of lighting - seems kind of flat to me.  I gave it a 6, so it was above average, but there''s a lack of contrast overall.  Perhaps a little dodging and burning would do the trick.  I sometimes have this same problem with my own photos - they just don''t pop well enough.', '2008-09-08 23:35:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943446, 709119, 60698, '<td valign="top">Very impressive! Love the colors! What a very clever title!!</td>', 'Very impressive! Love the colors! What a very clever title!!', '2008-09-08 23:39:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943486, 715495, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue:  N/A, image is monochrome.<br/> <br/>Brightness and contrast:  Image is well lit.  Contrast is good, highlights and shadows both hold good detail.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  the plane of focus may be a bit off, or depth of field made deeper.  For the current depth of field, the plane of focus is a bit too far back, as evidenced by the softness of the baby''s fingers on her right hand.<br/> <br/>At first I was unsure as to whether I liked Mom in soft focus.  In a way, it seems to diminish her role.  But at the same time, it helps say that this is not a snapshot.  That being said, it would have helped to comb Mom''s hair.  That does say snapshot, and the heavy strand of hair, distracts attention away from the subject.  If depth of field were shallower, it might soften it enough to overcome.  But at f/1.8 I don''t think you could get much softer, not matter what lens you used.  Perhaps the other answer is to darken the background even more so it is less competitive.  <br/> <br/>I like the pose.  A very peaceful moment for mother and child.  The child obviously feels very secure as evidenced by the relaxed position of the hand, and calm look on the face.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color Saturation and Hue:  N/A, image is monochrome. Brightness and contrast:  Image is well lit.  Contrast is good, highlights and shadows both hold good detail. Focus and depth of field:  the plane of focus may be a bit off, or depth of field made deeper.  For the current depth of field, the plane of focus is a bit too far back, as evidenced by the softness of the baby''s fingers on her right hand. At first I was unsure as to whether I liked Mom in soft focus.  In a way, it seems to diminish her role.  But at the same time, it helps say that this is not a snapshot.  That being said, it would have helped to comb Mom''s hair.  That does say snapshot, and the heavy strand of hair, distracts attention away from the subject.  If depth of field were shallower, it might soften it enough to overcome.  But at f/1.8 I don''t think you could get much softer, not matter what lens you used.  Perhaps the other answer is to darken the background even more so it is less competitive.   I like the pose.  A very peaceful moment for mother and child.  The child obviously feels very secure as evidenced by the relaxed position of the hand, and calm look on the face.', '2008-09-08 23:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4943495, 716736, 66515, '<td valign="top">This scored under 6? Incredible. I wouldn''t say the voters are stupid. Just a lot of them...<br/> <br/>Great sharp eyes. This fills the frame nicely. Not bad compositionally but not great either. Kinda hard to pose wildlife however :)<br/> <br/>The colors are nice without being oversaturated. <br/>You mention this shot in this thread:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=822097" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=822097</a> <br/> <br/>I can definitely see this in a wildlife magazine. <br/> <br/></td>', 'This scored under 6? Incredible. I wouldn''t say the voters are stupid. Just a lot of them... Great sharp eyes. This fills the frame nicely. Not bad compositionally but not great either. Kinda hard to pose wildlife however :) The colors are nice without being oversaturated. You mention this shot in this thread://www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&FORUM_THREAD_ID=822097  I can definitely see this in a wildlife magazine.  ', '2008-09-09 00:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
